       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change my answer, because the problem is the dose and not whether you meant it. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is five times the maximum dose of 200 mg/day. It could seriously harm the patient, and nothing in the information you gave me suggests a clinical reason for it.\n\nThe order also needs to come from the treating prescriber. A confirmation from someone outside that role doesn't meet that requirement.\n\nHere are the ways to move forward:\n- **The prescriber enters or confirms the order.** If there's an unusual clinical reason for this dose, they should discuss it with pharmacy and document it. The hospital's usual safety checks can then review it.\n- **A standard dose is intended.** Give me the dose, for example 50 mg, 100 mg, or 200 mg once daily. I'll enter it right away.\n\nI can enter an appropriate sertraline order as soon as I have a dose within the recommended range."
